id: pm-s79kel
title: "GH-665: schema migrations need derived idempotency keys and structured recovery"
description: "Make SDK schema-evolution planning ergonomic and deterministic when callers omit a migration id, allow side-effect-free dry-run planning, and route invalid migration input through the standard typed CLI recovery envelope."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:schema","area:sdk",gh-issue,migration
created_at: "2026-07-24T12:38:52.752Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T13:49:00.367Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-24T13:35:05.058Z"
author: codex-root-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Public SDK accepts an optional migration id and derives a deterministic workspace-and-operation-bound key; explicit ids preserve resume semantics; dry-run performs no workspace or journal write; CLI help/contracts describe the behavior; structured JSON and TOON recovery name the exact fix; packed consumer tests cover all migration kinds, repeated plans, explicit override, malformed input, and cross-workspace collision resistance."
parent: pm-dijg
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: codex-root-agent
severity: medium
repro_steps: "In a fresh workspace, run schema rename-type, rename-field, or remap-status without --migration-id, including --dry-run; the command emits a raw internal assertion and refuses to plan."
resolution: Schema evolution derives deterministic workspace/request-bound migration ids when omitted while preserving explicit orchestration ids.
expected_result: "SDK planning deterministically derives a stable idempotency key when omitted, explicit ids remain authoritative for resume, dry-run is side-effect-free, and invalid input returns the standard typed actionable error envelope."
actual_result: "The nominally optional migration id is de facto required and omission surfaces the raw string Schema migration migrationId must be non-empty, including for dry-run."
component: schema evolution SDK and CLI adapter
regression: true
customer_impact: Agents cannot discover or self-correct the headline schema-evolution workflow from runtime contracts and structured errors.
