comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:38:52.752Z",codex-root-agent,"Duplicate-check evidence: searched all statuses for GH-665, migrationId omission, dry-run planning, raw schema assertion, and structured recovery. Existing items shipped the migration engine and boundary classification; none owns this new first-use ergonomics regression."
  "2026-07-24T12:40:41.482Z",codex-root-agent,"Implementation start: claimed as an actively worked part of the broad SDK workspace mutation integrity PR. TDD scope covers deterministic id allocation, atomic stale-lock takeover, init cache and merge-fence ownership, schema migration idempotency/recovery, cross-runtime machine channels, and the fixed 10k performance gate."
  "2026-07-24T13:35:04.133Z",codex-root-agent,"Completion evidence: packed SDK/CLI consumer derived a stable auto- migration id over repeated dry-runs, produced a distinct id for the same request in a second workspace, preserved explicit external-orchestrator-42, applied rename-type without an explicit id, and losslessly rewrote the affected item to the new type. Unit coverage includes all migration kinds, malformed input, runtime/MCP adapters, and dry-run no-write boundaries. Final gate: 355 files / 6220 tests / literal 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-07-24T13:49:00.366Z",codex-root-agent,"Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/673 (broad SDK workspace mutation and migration primitives)."
